-- electrical.hm
-- hyperphysics | electrical law as a citable transport surface
--
-- LAYER INDEX DELIBERATELY UNASSIGNED.
-- hyperphysics' ground is not written. This file is NOT L0 and does not claim
-- to be. Naming it `L0_electrical.hm` would assert that circuit theory is the
-- ground of physics, which is false and which nothing here argues. When the
-- ground exists, this file gets re-indexed above it. Until then it carries no
-- index rather than a wrong one.
--
-- WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
-- Adjacent fields borrow the algebraic shape of electrical law. The combination
-- field metamathethicology.will_electrophysics transports the series-RLC form
-- onto the will tensor hyperethics declares. Left to itself each
-- borrower restates the law in its own words, the restatements drift, and the
-- phrase "this does not transport" loses its referent because no canonical
-- statement of the borrowed law survives. So the laws live here and borrowers
-- cite them by name.
--
-- Status: FORM for the transport interface and the parameter-independence
--         statement; the physics itself is CITED, not derived. Every law below
--         is textbook classical circuit theory in the lumped-element
--         approximation. Nothing here is new physics and nothing is offered as
--         new physics.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION I: QUANTITIES
-- =============================================================================

primitive Quantity :: Type
    -- charge Q, current I, current-rate dI/dt,
    -- resistance R, inductance L, capacitance C, voltage V.
    -- Each carries its SI unit as data, because a transport must be able to
    -- name the unit it is declining to carry.

derive d-derivative-chain:
    -- Q, I, dI/dt are NOT three independent quantities.
    --   I      = dQ/dt
    --   dI/dt  = d2Q/dt2
    -- They are the zeroth, first, and second time derivatives of one quantity,
    -- and that exhausts the temporal structure of a circuit's state.
    -- This is the structural fact the will transport's temporal components land
    -- on, and it is the reason that part of the transport is forced rather than
    -- chosen: once 'past' is charge, 'present' and 'future' are not free. The
    -- ordering on the will side is hyperethics' own d-temporal-chain, derived
    -- there without reference to this file; the transport borrows it.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION II: LAWS
-- Each law carries: statement, form, quantities, validity, failure modes.
-- The failure modes are the load-bearing part. A transported form inherits the
-- failure modes of its source unless the borrower argues otherwise, and the
-- borrower cannot argue against a statement it never read.
-- =============================================================================

law ohm:                 V = I * R
law faraday-lenz:        V = L * dI/dt
law capacitor:           V = Q / C         -- equivalently C = Q / V
law self-inductance:     emf = -L * dI/dt  -- own changing current; Lenz sign
law mutual-inductance:   emf_2 = -M * dI_1/dt  -- ANOTHER circuit's current
law kirchhoff-voltage:   sum of drops = applied
law series-rlc:          L * d2Q/dt2 + R * dQ/dt + (1/C) * Q = V

derive d-series-is-composed:
    -- series-rlc is not a fifth independent law. It is kirchhoff-voltage applied
    -- to faraday-lenz, ohm, and capacitor.
    -- CONSEQUENCE, enforced in code: a borrower of series-rlc inherits the
    -- failure modes of all four, not of one.

derive d-self-versus-mutual:
    -- self-inductance and mutual-inductance have the SAME algebraic form and
    -- differ only in whose changing current does the inducing.
    -- This distinction carries no extra mathematics and is entirely about
    -- source. It is the electrical reading of the distinction hyperethics uses
    -- to separate an invariant will arising in an entity's own changing willing
    -- from one arising in another's -- a distinction hyperethics states in
    -- will-native terms and does not need this law to state. The point is that
    -- the separation is invisible in the form alone -- exactly why a borrower
    -- must state which one it means.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION III: PARAMETER INDEPENDENCE
-- =============================================================================

axiom ax-parameters-independent:
    -- In a series RLC circuit, R, L, and C are INDEPENDENT parameters. An
    -- inductor and a capacitor are physically distinct components; any one may
    -- be varied with the others held fixed.
    -- Stated explicitly because it is precisely where a borrower may depart.

derive d-constrained-transport-is-not-onto:
    -- A field constraining its analogue of C to be a function of its analogue
    -- of L has a SMALLER parameter space than the circuit.
    -- CONSEQUENCE: the transport is not onto. Not every circuit corresponds to
    -- a state of that field, so circuit intuitions about independently tuning
    -- the two do not carry over.
    -- This is not a defect. It is a structural difference that must be
    -- DECLARED rather than discovered later by a reader who assumed the
    -- parameter spaces matched.
    -- LIVE INSTANCE: metamathethicology.will_electrophysics declares exactly
    -- this departure. Its 'constant will' is bound to invariant will rather than
    -- free, on the user declaration that capacitance is invariant will's
    -- constant of charge.
    -- See Transport.constrains_parameters.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION IV: THE TRANSPORT INTERFACE
-- =============================================================================

primitive Transport :: Type
    -- What a borrowing field must declare, at the point of borrowing:
    --   1. which law, BY NAME, so the claim has a fixed referent;
    --   2. what form the law takes in the target field;
    --   3. what the borrowing transports;
    --   4. what it does NOT transport, concretely enough to name a unit or a
    --      mechanism of the cited law;
    --   5. whether the target constrains a parameter the source leaves free,
    --      with a reason.
    -- Item 5 is the one usually missed. See d-constrained-transport-is-not-onto.

axiom ax-units-do-not-transport:
    -- SI units attach to the physical quantity and its measurement procedure,
    -- never to the algebraic form. No transport carries a unit.
    -- Enforced: `validate` rejects a disclaimer that names neither a unit nor a
    -- mechanism of the law it cites. A borrower cannot satisfy the interface
    -- with a general assurance; it must decline something specific.

non-derive nd-validation-is-not-soundness:
    -- `validate` checks that the required declarations were MADE and are about
    -- the law they claim to be about. It does NOT check that the transport is
    -- sound, and no function in this package can. A perfectly declared
    -- transport may be a bad analogy.
    -- This limit is stated here so that passing validation is never mistaken
    -- for having earned the borrowing.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION V: GRADUATION CRITERION
-- =============================================================================

graduation:
    -- GC-1: laws stated once, with validity and failure modes as data.
    --       DISCHARGED.
    -- GC-2: composition tracked, so a borrower of the series form inherits all
    --       four constituents' failure modes. DISCHARGED -- inherited_failure_modes.
    -- GC-3: an interface that makes a borrowing checkable rather than implicit.
    --       DISCHARGED as a record; see nd-validation-is-not-soundness for what
    --       that does and does not buy.
    -- GC-4: a criterion for when a transport is SOUND rather than merely
    --       declared. NOT DISCHARGED, and this is the real open problem of the
    --       package.
    -- GC-5: hyperphysics' own ground, of which circuit theory would be a
    --       consequence rather than a starting point. NOT WRITTEN.
    -- GC-6: units and dimensional analysis. NOT DISCHARGED. Numeric functions
    --       here take dimensionless magnitudes; unit handling is the caller's.
    --
    -- Three of six discharged, and the two that matter most are open. This
    -- package does not graduate as a physics; it graduates as a citation
    -- surface, which is all it currently claims to be.
